### Figure S2: Season

Seasonal time trends reflecting the average concentrations of individual analytes (ng/mL) and molar sums (µM) of contemporary and emerging chemicals measured in mid-pregnancy urine samples and corrected with specific gravity among pregnant women in the Atlanta Maternal Child Cohort from 2016-2019 (N=168).  

Note: Each point represents the geometric average concentration of month of sample collection with 95% confidence intervals. Seasons are indicated by shading (winter, blue: December, January, February, spring, green: March, April, May, summer, pink: June, July, August, fall, red: September October, November). Five chemicals were the only well detected analyte in their chemical group, and as such are presented individually. This includes the pentachlorophenol (halogenated phenol), 2,4-dichlorophenoxtace (fungicide and herbicide), bisphenol S (bisphenol), 3,5,6-trichloro-pyridinol (insecticide), and mono (carboxyisoctyl) phthalate (di-2-ethylhexyl metabolites (diisononyl phthalate metabolites (DINP)).

